    "Question #: 2": {
      "Title": "Exam GMAT Section 2 Quantitative topic 1 question 238 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The angles of a triangle are in the ratio of 3: 2: 1. The largest angle in the triangle is:"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. 36."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. 45."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. 72."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. 90."
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. 108."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: E \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The sum of all the angles is 180. Divide 180 by 6 (3+2+1) and well get 36; this is the size of the smallest angle. The largest angle is three times bigger, thus 36 x 3"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "= 108 degrees."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
